Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:47:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Follow her out of the door at walking pace, then rise
 from her right in one smooth curve (exit camera B5).

Funning rejected B4: the lens surged from ~0.9 to ~6 m/s right after the doorway and lifted in a step.
B5 builds the exit as her low-passed root plus an offset whose bearing, radius and height blend door ->
follow -> cameraIsland with smootherstep weights, so position, velocity and acceleration are continuous;
the doorway key's velocity and acceleration are carried into the follow and fade out. Her exit path walks
~2.3 m straight out before curving onto exit_path_17. Settle 5.5 s, door 86.4 (as B4), X2/O back to the
original x, crossOutEnd 0.1 m to her right. Delete crane.pace.b5 to roll back to B4.

Not pushed. Offline flow_sim only; exit-overlap / exit-cruise-real / composition snapshot still encode the
B4-era cruise contract and fail by design.
